&lt;li&gt;Experience with industrial compressed air systems and maintenance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with carpentry maintenance tasks, including routine sheetrock/drywall installation and/or repair, window replacement, cabinet/countertop replacement, painting/texturing (interior and exterior), and door/hardware installation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read instructions and blueprints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with project management software, MS Excel, Word, or other project tracking software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills - MS Outlook and Teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand and follow specific instructions and procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated, works well with others and autonomously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Safety training and use of forklifts, scissor lifts, cranes &amp;amp; hoists, and fall protection equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to work all shifts and available for overtime, weekends and holiday as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid Texas driver&#39;s license&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stand: Up to 10 hours per day&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
